pinyon-shift-fh1-render-test-v1
# clock-hz 60
# #531 observation route, from the Gauntlet free-roam pinned seed.
# Launch with --pinyon_shift_cheats=true --present_hdr=false, the desired
# --pinyon_shift_fh1_render_fps_limit=30, 60 or 120, and
# --pinyon_shift_fh1_shadows=false (repeat with true). Use a fresh private state
# for each run. Record video: the sparse captures only confirm the scene.
# The 60 Hz logical clock keeps the 20s-140s night window the same length
# at every output rate. Output-clock wait steps cannot be used with it.
# Passing the runner is not a flicker verdict: review the video and confirm
# that oncoming traffic actually appeared.
# See docs/native-renderer/HEADLIGHT_FLICKER.md.
input 0 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
cvar 1 cheat_time_of_day 23
cvar 3 disable_bloom false
input 360 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 366 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 480 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 486 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 600 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 606 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 720 1000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 726 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
input 1200 0000 0 80 0 0 0 0
capture 1200 night-start
input 1800 0000 0 0 0 0 0 0
capture 2400 night-40s
capture 3600 night-60s
capture 4800 night-80s
capture 6000 night-100s
capture 7200 night-120s
capture 8400 night-140s
stop 8500
